{"kind":"issue","id":103,"uid":"01M2HAW2B9Z6M3JYFDBW3NP104","project_id":29,"project_uid":"01M2HAW1EWEKTGTHM0NMB4CB1S","short_id":"p104","title":"run-131: One kata project per target — the launcher seeds it idempotently, and a proof that runs a sibling's file is an edge","body":"**Claim:** One kata project per target repository, not per run: the launcher files a run's tasks as issues into the target's project, each carrying its `Consumes:`/`Produces:` edges as `--blocked-by`, plus the edge the compiler derives from a `Run:` or `Check:` that names a path in a sibling task's Files (the seam run-127's task 1 failed on — see the 2026-09-14 comment on #810). The plan stays an idempotent seed: re-filing the same plan creates nothing twice. (quoted from #978)","status":"open","author":"launch","metadata":{"base":"c3c8fa9bbf1d6a339b81a81234a41066720dd94f","closes":[978],"run":131,"target":"popmechanic/ultrapowers"},"revision":1,"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:28:29.802Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T01:28:29.802Z","qualified_id":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-131#p104","child_counts":{"open":4,"total":4}}
